From 99ee2546cf73e3b4f890a50924e21676d57d16f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@local>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 19:28:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Remora: forward-port "protect sensitive data on about page"
 to AOSP 17
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces upstream 0079 (Reapply: Settings: Protect sensitive data on the about
page), which cannot apply: AOSP 17 restructured ImeiPreference and
SimEidPreference onto the new preference-metadata API, so the file the Lineage
patch was written against no longer exists in that shape.

The Lineage change itself is small — mask IMEI and EID behind "Tap to show info"
and reveal on click. The conflict is entirely structural:

  * AOSP 17 added supportsWrite / valueType / storage() and its own getSummary().
    Kept, with only getSummary() replaced by the masked string.
  * The click listener lost Lineage's `imei` and `slotIndex` locals. AOSP 17
    computes slotId from an ImeiData list instead, so the reveal now reads
    imeiList[index].imei and keeps AOSP's slotId for the dialog. Guarded by the
    same index bound AOSP already applies, so a short list cannot throw.

R.string.device_info_protected_single_press is already added earlier in the
series (res/values/strings.xml), so no new resource is needed.

NOT COMPILE-VERIFIED. Written while a build held the tree, so this has not been
through kotlinc. Verify before relying on it.
